  {
    "index": 3,
    "hash": "PuL8J+9nKjgYgNdYqEmWk9br6uw=",
    "timestampUtcMs": "2026-08-20T10:34:05.428Z",
    "action": {
      "type": "SET_CONTENT",
      "input": {
        "content": "The stated criteria are that the complementary software \"is sufficiently open-source\", \"is deployed within the consultancy projects\", and \"offers us an ecosystem that we can tap into\".\n\nEach does distinct work. Open source makes integration possible without a commercial negotiation and makes the gap inspectable. Deployment inside consultancy projects means the integration reaches clients through someone else's existing delivery motion. The ecosystem requirement is about reach: a partner directory or user community converts one integration into many conversations.\n\nTogether they define the shape of the play \u2014 Powerhouse attaches to software the consultancy already installs, so the consultancy is the channel and the end client is reached through it.",
        "updatedAt": "2026-08-20T10:34:05.428593Z"
      },
      "timestampUtcMs": "2026-08-20T10:34:05.428597Z"
    }
  },
